---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service" description="B2B Terms of Service governing the use of Yield Force AI sales automation platform, operated by Gaia Holdings Limited, incorporated in Uganda.">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-slate-800 pb-8">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-blue-500/30 bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 text-xs font-medium mb-4">
        B2B Commercial Terms
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-3">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
        Effective date: <span class="text-slate-300 font-medium">22 September 2026</span> · Last updated: <span class="text-slate-300 font-medium">22 September 2026</span>
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-2">
        <strong class="text-slate-400">Yield Force</strong> is a trading name of <strong class="text-slate-400">Gaia Holdings Limited</strong>, a company incorporated and registered in Uganda.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-slate-300 space-y-10 text-sm leading-relaxed">

      <!-- Preamble -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">Preamble</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms of Service (the "<strong class="text-white">Agreement</strong>") form a legally binding contract between <strong class="text-white">Gaia Holdings Limited</strong> (incorporated in Uganda under the Companies Act, 2012, trading as <strong class="text-white">Yield Force</strong> — "<strong class="text-white">Supplier</strong>", "<strong class="text-white">we</strong>", "<strong class="text-white">us</strong>", "<strong class="text-white">our</strong>") and the merchant entity accessing or using the Yield Force platform ("<strong class="text-white">Merchant</strong>", "<strong class="text-white">Customer</strong>", "<strong class="text-white">you</strong>").
        </p>
        <p>
          By installing the Yield Force application via the Shopify App Store, creating an account, or otherwise accessing the platform, you agree to be bound by this Agreement in its entirety.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-blue-900/20 border border-blue-700/30 rounded-xl p-4 text-slate-300 text-xs leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-white">This Agreement is a business-to-business contract.</strong> By accepting these terms, the Merchant warrants that it enters into this Agreement solely in the course of its trade, business, craft, or profession — <strong class="text-white">not as a consumer</strong>. Consumer protection legislation applicable to consumer contracts does not govern this Agreement.
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Document Hierarchy -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">Document Hierarchy</h2>
        <p>Where any conflict exists between documents forming part of this Agreement, the following order of precedence applies:</p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-300">
          <li>Executed Enterprise Order Form or Schedule (if any)</li>
          <li>Data Processing Addendum (DPA) — solely with respect to personal data processing</li>
          <li>These Terms of Service (Master Agreement)</li>
          <li>Acceptable Use Policy (Appendix A)</li>
          <li>Product documentation and specifications</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <!-- 1. Definitions -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">1. Definitions</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="min-w-full text-left border border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden text-xs">
            <thead class="bg-slate-900/80 text-slate-300 border-b border-slate-800">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Term</th>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Meaning</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 bg-slate-900/30">
              <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Services</td><td class="p-3">The Yield Force AI-powered sales automation platform, including all Zones (0–7), agent swarms, APIs, dashboards, and integrations</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Platform</td><td class="p-3">The software, infrastructure, and systems operated by Gaia Holdings Limited to deliver the Services</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Merchant Data</td><td class="p-3">All data, content, product catalogs, policies, and knowledge base materials uploaded by the Merchant</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Customer Personal Data</td><td class="p-3">Personal data of end consumers (shoppers) processed by the Supplier on behalf of the Merchant</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Subscription Fee</td><td class="p-3">The recurring base fee payable for access to the Platform</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Performance Fee</td><td class="p-3">The variable fee based on Attributed Net Sales generated through the Platform</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Attributed Net Sales</td><td class="p-3">Net product sales (excluding VAT, discounts, and shipping) arising from Yield Force-assisted conversational checkouts within the attribution window, as defined in Clause 7</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">WABA</td><td class="p-3">WhatsApp Business Account — the Merchant's registered business messaging account on Meta's WhatsApp Cloud API</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Sovereign Key</td><td class="p-3">The per-tenant cryptographic identifier enforcing multi-tenant data isolation within the Platform</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Zone 5 Governance Portal</td><td class="p-3">The Merchant-facing administrative interface for supervising, overriding, and configuring AI agent behaviour</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Insolvency Event</td><td class="p-3">Any of: administration, liquidation, receivership, voluntary arrangement, winding-up, or analogous proceedings under the Uganda Insolvency Act, 2011 or equivalent applicable law</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. License Grant -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">2. License Grant and Permitted Use</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">2.1 License</h3>
          <p>Subject to payment of applicable fees and compliance with this Agreement, the Supplier grants the Merchant a <strong class="text-white">non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable</strong> right to access and use the Services during the Subscription Term, solely for the Merchant's internal business operations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">2.2 Tenant Isolation</h3>
          <p>The Merchant's access to the Platform is strictly bounded by its provisioned Sovereign Key. Any attempt to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Circumvent multi-tenant data isolation boundaries;</li>
            <li>Access, probe, or extract data belonging to another tenant;</li>
            <li>Reverse-engineer API endpoints, prompt architectures, or AI model weights;</li>
          </ul>
          <p>constitutes a <strong class="text-white">non-curable material breach</strong> of this Agreement, entitling the Supplier to terminate immediately and seek injunctive relief without further notice.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">2.3 Authorised Users</h3>
          <p>The Merchant is solely responsible for all activity conducted under its credentials, including activity by its staff, agents, and any third parties (such as marketing agencies) granted access to the Zone 4/5 dashboards.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Services & Availability -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">3. Services, Availability, and Service Levels</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">3.1 Availability Target</h3>
          <p>The Supplier targets <strong class="text-white">99.5% monthly uptime</strong> for the core ingress and routing layer (Zone 2 Refinery Gateway), measured on a rolling 30-day calendar basis, excluding Scheduled Maintenance, Force Majeure, and third-party platform outages.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">3.2 Exclusions</h3>
          <p>Availability measurements exclude downtime caused by:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Scheduled maintenance (with prior notice where practicable);</li>
            <li>Emergency security patches;</li>
            <li>Failures of Meta Platforms APIs or Shopify APIs;</li>
            <li>Acts of Force Majeure (see Clause 13);</li>
            <li>Merchant network, browser, or device failures;</li>
            <li>The Merchant's failure to maintain accounts in good standing with Meta or Shopify.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">3.3 Service Credits (Sole and Exclusive Remedy)</h3>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="min-w-full text-left border border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden text-xs">
              <thead class="bg-slate-900/80 text-slate-300 border-b border-slate-800">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Monthly Uptime</th>
                  <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Credit</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 bg-slate-900/30">
                <tr><td class="p-3">99.0% – 99.49%</td><td class="p-3">5% of monthly Subscription Fee</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3">95.0% – 98.99%</td><td class="p-3">10% of monthly Subscription Fee</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3">Below 95.0%</td><td class="p-3">15% of monthly Subscription Fee</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>Service Credits are applied against the Merchant's next invoice and are the <strong class="text-white">Merchant's sole and exclusive remedy</strong> for availability failures, except where the Platform falls below 95% availability for three (3) consecutive calendar months, in which case either party may terminate on 30 days' written notice.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. Term & Termination -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">4. Term, Renewal, and Termination</h2>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">4.1 Term</h3>
          <p>This Agreement commences on the date the Merchant accepts these Terms and continues for successive monthly (or annual, if selected) billing cycles ("<strong class="text-white">Subscription Term</strong>"), automatically renewing unless cancelled in accordance with Clause 4.3.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">4.2 Auto-Renewal</h3>
          <p>Subscriptions renew automatically at the end of each Subscription Term unless the Merchant cancels at least <strong class="text-white">30 days</strong> prior to renewal (or uninstalls the app via the Shopify Admin before the end of the current billing cycle).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">4.3 Termination for Cause</h3>
          <p>Either party may terminate this Agreement with immediate effect upon written notice if:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>The other party commits a <strong class="text-white">material breach</strong> that is incapable of remedy, or fails to remedy a remediable breach within <strong class="text-white">30 days</strong> of written notice specifying the breach; or</li>
            <li>The other party undergoes an <strong class="text-white">Insolvency Event</strong>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">4.4 Suspension and Immediate Termination by the Supplier</h3>
          <p>The Supplier may suspend or terminate the Merchant's access immediately, without prior notice or liability, if:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>The Merchant breaches the Acceptable Use Policy (Appendix A);</li>
            <li>The Merchant fails to pay any sum due and the sum remains outstanding for more than 7 days after the due date;</li>
            <li>Meta or Shopify requires suspension in connection with the Merchant's account or conduct; or</li>
            <li>Continued provision of Services would expose the Supplier to legal, regulatory, or reputational risk.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">4.5 Post-Termination Transition</h3>
          <p>Upon termination or expiry of this Agreement:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>The Merchant's access to the Platform terminates immediately;</li>
            <li>The Merchant is granted a <strong class="text-white">30-day grace period</strong> to retrieve historical conversation logs, attribution analytics, and Merchant Data via the Zone 5 export tools;</li>
            <li>Following 30 days, the Supplier will permanently purge all Merchant Data, Customer Personal Data, and tenant secrets from the Platform in accordance with Clause 9.8 and GDPR Article 28(3)(g);</li>
            <li>All accrued fees remain due and payable.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. AI Operation -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">5. AI Operation, Probabilistic Output, and Human Oversight</h2>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">5.1 Probabilistic Technology</h3>
          <p>The Merchant acknowledges that the Services utilise artificial intelligence, machine learning, and large language models ("<strong class="text-white">AI Systems</strong>") to generate conversational outputs. The Merchant understands that AI Systems produce <strong class="text-white">probabilistic outputs</strong> that may occasionally contain inaccuracies, omissions, errors, or unintended content ("<strong class="text-white">Hallucinations</strong>"). The Supplier makes no warranty that AI-generated outputs will be error-free or achieve any specific commercial conversion rate or sales volume.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">5.2 Merchant as Publisher and Principal</h3>
          <p>The Merchant agrees that all communications sent by the AI Systems through the Merchant's connected messaging channels (WhatsApp WABA, Instagram profile, Facebook Page, Shopify storefront) are transmitted <strong class="text-white">on behalf of the Merchant as principal</strong>. The Merchant is the sole legal author and publisher of all such communications. The AI Systems have no authority to amend the Merchant's published prices, terms of sale, return policies, or consumer warranties beyond data synced from the Merchant's Shopify catalog. All binding contracts of sale are formed exclusively upon the end customer completing checkout on Shopify's settlement rail.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">5.3 Human Oversight and Governance Obligations</h3>
          <p>The Supplier provides the Zone 5 Governance Portal, including a dual-mode Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) override queue, real-time conversation monitoring, and emergency agent kill switches.</p>
          <p>The Merchant <strong class="text-white">covenants</strong> to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Maintain accurate, lawful, and current product information and policies in the Knowledge Canvas;</li>
            <li>Regularly monitor active conversation threads and high-value buying interactions;</li>
            <li>Promptly activate override controls or the emergency kill switch upon detecting anomalous AI behaviour;</li>
            <li>Ensure staff responsible for supervision are adequately trained in platform governance.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The Merchant's failure to maintain active supervision of the AI Systems is entirely at the Merchant's own risk.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">5.4 EU AI Act Disclosure Obligation</h3>
          <p>Under <strong class="text-white">Article 50 of the EU AI Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689)</strong>, the Merchant, acting as the <strong class="text-white">Deployer</strong> of an AI system interacting directly with natural persons, must ensure that EU-based natural persons are clearly informed at the commencement of each interaction that they are communicating with an AI system.</p>
          <p>The Supplier equips all agents with default AI identification disclosures. The Merchant <strong class="text-white">covenants not to disable, tamper with, or remove</strong> such mandatory disclosures for interactions with consumers in the EU or any other jurisdiction where AI transparency obligations apply.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">5.5 Merchant Indemnity — Conversational Content</h3>
          <p>The Merchant shall <strong class="text-white">defend, indemnify, and hold harmless</strong> Gaia Holdings Limited, its affiliates, directors, officers, employees, and agents from and against all claims, liabilities, losses, damages, fines, penalties, costs, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising out of or in connection with:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Any communication, advice, statement, recommendation, or representation sent to an end consumer by the AI Systems via the Merchant's connected accounts;</li>
            <li>Any investigation or enforcement action by a consumer protection authority or advertising standards body (including the ACM and AP in the Netherlands, or the PDPO in Uganda) relating to the Merchant's products or conversational marketing;</li>
            <li>Any product liability or consumer dispute arising from orders initiated or fulfilled through the Services.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. Third-Party Platform Dependencies -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">6. Third-Party Platform Dependencies</h2>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">6.1 No Control Over Third Parties</h3>
          <p>The Services integrate with, depend upon, and interoperate with APIs hosted by <strong class="text-white">Meta Platforms, Inc. / Meta Platforms Ireland Limited</strong> ("<strong class="text-white">Meta</strong>") and <strong class="text-white">Shopify Inc.</strong> ("<strong class="text-white">Shopify</strong>"). The Supplier has no ownership or operational control over such third-party services.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">6.2 Disclaimer of Upstream Disruptions</h3>
          <p>The Supplier disclaims all liability for any disruption, latency, data loss, dropped webhooks, degraded performance, or total outage caused by or attributable to Meta, Shopify, or any third-party foundational model provider.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">6.3 Platform Enforcement and Continued Payment Obligations</h3>
          <p>The Supplier bears <strong class="text-white">zero liability</strong> for any decision by Meta or Shopify to throttle messaging limits, degrade WhatsApp phone number quality ratings, suspend, ban, or restrict the Merchant's WABA, Instagram account, Facebook Page, or Shopify storefront, or deprecate APIs or alter rate limits.</p>
          <p>Any such third-party enforcement action does <strong class="text-white">not</strong> constitute a breach by the Supplier, does <strong class="text-white">not</strong> give the Merchant any right to a refund, and does <strong class="text-white">not</strong> relieve the Merchant of its obligation to pay all applicable Subscription Fees and Performance Fees.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">6.4 Merchant Policy Compliance Warranties</h3>
          <p>The Merchant warrants that it holds active accounts in good standing with Meta and Shopify, and shall at all times comply with Meta Terms of Service, WhatsApp Business Messaging Policy, WhatsApp Commerce Policy, Shopify Terms of Service, and applicable AI model provider acceptable use policies.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 7. Fees & Billing -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">7. Fees, Billing, and Payment</h2>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">7.1 Fee Structure</h3>
          <p>Yield Force operates on a hybrid pricing model:</p>
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong class="text-white">Subscription Fee:</strong> Fixed recurring monthly or annual charge.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Performance Fee:</strong> Variable fee based on Attributed Net Sales (rate per applicable pricing plan or Order Form).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Usage and Overage Charges:</strong> Additional charges for volume or channel capacity exceeding the Merchant's tier allowance.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">7.2 Attributed Net Sales Definition</h3>
          <p>"<strong class="text-white">Attributed Net Sales</strong>" means net product sales (gross merchandise value minus applied discounts, excluding VAT/sales tax and shipping) recorded against Shopify orders that are:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Tagged with the Yield Force attribution identifier (<code class="text-blue-300">#YF-Converted</code>);</li>
            <li>Completed within a <strong class="text-white">7-day last-touch attribution window</strong> following an active conversational interaction in which a Closer agent generated or updated a cart permalink containing the Yield Force referral parameter (<code class="text-blue-300">?ref=yf&tid=&lt;thread_id&gt;</code>); and</li>
            <li>Not subsequently cancelled, refunded, or returned in full within the <strong class="text-white">14-day rolling reconciliation window</strong>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">7.3 Shopify App Store Billing</h3>
          <p>For merchants accessing Yield Force via the Shopify App Store:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Subscription Fees are billed via the <strong class="text-white">Shopify Recurring Application Charge API</strong>;</li>
            <li>Performance Fees and overage charges are recorded via the <strong class="text-white">Shopify Usage Charge API</strong> against the Merchant's pre-authorised monthly spending cap.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">7.4 VAT and Tax</h3>
          <p>All fees are quoted <strong class="text-white">exclusive</strong> of Value Added Tax (VAT), Dutch <em>omzetbelasting</em> (BTW), and all other applicable taxes and duties.</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong class="text-white">Netherlands-based Merchants:</strong> Dutch BTW at the prevailing rate will be added to all invoices, or the reverse-charge mechanism will apply where the Merchant provides a valid VAT identification number.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Other EU Merchants with valid EU VAT ID:</strong> The <strong class="text-white">reverse charge mechanism</strong> applies pursuant to Article 196 of EU Council Directive 2006/112/EC. If the Merchant fails to provide a valid EU VAT registration number, applicable local VAT will be charged.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">7.5 Payment Default and Late Payment Interest</h3>
          <p>If a payment method fails or a Shopify billing invoice is declined:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>The Merchant has a <strong class="text-white">7-day grace period</strong> to resolve the billing failure;</li>
            <li>Following 7 days of non-payment, the Supplier may suspend conversational agent routing without liability;</li>
            <li>Following 30 days of non-payment, the Supplier may terminate this Agreement pursuant to Clause 4.3;</li>
            <li>Overdue amounts accrue interest at a commercially agreed rate from the due date until actual payment, compounding monthly, pursuant to the Uganda Contracts Act, 2010. Where proceedings are brought in the Netherlands, statutory commercial interest under <strong class="text-white">Article 6:119a of the Dutch Civil Code (BW)</strong> and statutory debt collection costs under <strong class="text-white">Article 6:96(4) BW</strong> (minimum €40) may apply.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">7.6 Cancellation and Refund Policy</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>The Merchant may cancel at any time by uninstalling the application via the Shopify Admin or by providing 30 days' written notice for direct subscription contracts.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">All fees paid are strictly non-refundable.</strong> No pro-rata refunds or credits will be issued for partial months, unused conversational capacity, or downtime attributable to third-party platform actions.</li>
            <li>Unused conversation capacity expires at the end of each billing cycle and does not roll over.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 8. Intellectual Property -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">8. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">8.1 Supplier's Platform Rights</h3>
          <p>Gaia Holdings Limited (or its licensors) retains all right, title, and interest — including all applicable intellectual property rights — in and to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>The Yield Force platform, multi-zone architecture (Zones 0–7), LangGraph multi-agent swarm implementations, refinery gateway, and multi-tenant security infrastructure;</li>
            <li>All system prompt templates, agent directives, routing heuristics, and algorithmic optimisation models (including Thompson Sampling Bayesian frameworks);</li>
            <li>All Platform documentation, API definitions, user interface designs, and codebases;</li>
            <li>Aggregated, anonymised telemetry and operational performance benchmarks that do not contain Customer Personal Data or identifiable Merchant trade secrets.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
